hich when pulled from this box would  bring upon destruction to this entire  Kingdom and thus should never fall into  the hands of evil hello there  [Music]  but my leech can you imagine the  potential this technology has for this  kingdom for years to come  nope bury it all oh and be a good man  and chase away the sheikah chaps that  helped us in the war but my league  like I said idiots there seems to be  something strange going on with Queens  in zelda lore in general as we never  actually see them they are always absent  we have seen kings in the flash as early  as a link to the past and subsequently  in the Wind Waker and to Kings in the  Minish Cap that being the spirit of King  Gustav and the present-day King Dahl  tiss yet in all instances no Queen by  their side nor are they even referenced  or mentioned ever  that is until breath of the wild even  though we don't know what she looked  like or even her name this is the first  time in the history of zelda canon that  the existence of a queen is actually  acknowledged proof of this lies within  both creating a champion which refers to  Zelda's mother as Queen on multiple  occasions as well as our BOCES diary in  the champions ballad dlc in witcher Bosa  states quote it is always a pleasure to  see the queen of hyrule I told her that  zelda is sure to grow up into a  dignified and beautiful queen just like  her mother  now fantasy stories and fairy tales tend  to simplify the aspect of royalty with  good reason of course since a lot of it  is partially aimed towards kids we  simply have a king and a queen easy as  that in real life however royal families  are a lot more complicated I won't turn  this into an entire history lesson but  one of the basic things to know is that  there isn't always a king and queen  involved for instance Britain has a  queen but no king the Netherlands has  both but why this has to do with  historical and patriarchal traditions  it's a bit similar to the old fashioned  custom where a woman inherits her  husband's last name upon marriage when a  woman marries a king she tends to  receive the ceremonial title of Queen or  queen consort but let's just keep it  simple however when it's the other way  around the man does not inherit the  title of king but rather Prince there's  only a few rare examples where an  exception was made and the husband was  granted the title of king which  why Queen Elizabeth's husband is called  Prince Philip well technically his full  title is this but let's not go there  it's Prince and just in case you were  wondering since this is a Japanese  series it works the same way in Asian  cultures as well except here instead of  a king or queen  it's called Emperor or Empress but the  title of prince and princess are the  same going back to zelda as stated  before she obviously has been queen in  the past just not for us the player to  see after the Minish Cap she would no  doubt be crowned after king daughters  passes or gives up the title after  ocarina of time she would eventually  become queen in all three timeline  branches and in the downfall and idol  branch rather quickly as the king of  hyrule is implied to have died during  ganondorf's attack on hyrule castle  furthermore after the events of a Link  to the Past she will eventually become  Queen which leads into a link between  worlds in Phantom Hourglass after the  founding of new Hyrule and after the  defeat of Ganondorf in Twilight Princess  just to name a few in each game where we  see a descendent of Zelda it's clear  that at some point before all of this  the previous incarnation of zelda  married and eventually had offspring  since the bloodline of goddess hylia  would have ended if she didn't in  between some games there's even multiple  generations of royalty as an example in  Spirit Tracks the Zelda we see here is  not the daughter of tetra but rather her  granddaughter keep that in mind for  later the closest we've seen Zelda to  becoming Queen was in Twilight Princess  this game is set to take place more than  a hundred years after Ocarina of Time  and Majora's Mask and there's no  appearance or even mention of any other  royal family members besides Zelda  herself she seems to be at the steering  wheel alone and has the soldiers under  her command yet is still referred to as  princess multiple times in game she's  also the one to issue the surrender of  the kingdom to Zant something a princess  wouldn't have the authority to do under  normal circumstances turns out that  Zelda was on the brink of becoming Queen  but the invasion of Zant prevented this  from happening without an official  coronation ever taking place she  remained with the title of princess  throughout the events of the game as a  matter of fact it's highly likely that  the gift link was supposed to deliver to  hyrule castle at the beginning of the  game which is the sword crafted by  Russell was part of Zelda's crowning  ceremony and we find even more  information of this in a more unusual  place that being that's why lie princess  trading card deck which didn't even know  existed to be completely honest the deck  holds a total of 86 cards of which 22  are character cards the description on  Zelda's card reads she is shortly to be  crowned queen of Hyrule which indicates  that the previous king or queen has  recently passed away making her next in  line for the title so close but yet so  far when I said that we've never seen  Zelda as Queen in game that's actually  not completely true we have it's just  that it's not canon in Hyrule warriors  zelda is confirmed to be queen by  producer yusuke hayashi who states quote  in Hyrule warriors Princess Zelda is  actually Queen Zelda  she has an army as a queen would and  link is a trainee but as the story  unfolds the relationship between the two  greatly changes additionally our numa  also mentions this in an interview quote  we definitely change how zelda is used  and position her where it's best for the  experience that is as Queen and one of  the playable characters in Hyrule  warriors we also have another instance  in which we see Zelda becoming Queen  however this one is even less canonical  than Hyrule warriors it comes from the a  Link to the Past manga written by  Shotaro Ishinomori and published in 1992  it's an alternate version of the events  from a Link to the Past at the end of  the story  Zelda has become Queen and Link is the  head of the Royal Guards and Knights of  Hyrule it even states that this success  is bittersweet as their duties keep them  apart even though they were one so close  and sharing an adventure and even coming  together in dreams again this is of  course not part of the main line zelda  canon it's nice to know it exists but  i'm not counting it as a confirmation  for the title of queen for our beloved  princess now i don't want to overthink  this too much since we are dealing with  a fantasy series here but one thing that  i started to wonder about while writing  this script was how does all this tie  together with the bloodline of goddess  hylia historically we don't know whose  eldest previous husbands were though it  is hinted that in some cases this could  have been linked himself  so for this example let's satisfy the  selling fans among you for a little bit  my question would be what if Lincoln  Zelda had a son and only a son does the  power of the goddess continue but simply  skips the son until eventually a female  is born later down the line because  similar to how the hero is always male  the one to possess an awakened highly a  sealing power has always been female so  this seems to be a key element to this  whole goddess thing  the reason I'm posing this question is  because going back to spirit tracks  during the final confrontation with  maladies Zelda prays to receive the  power from goddess hylia but not from  her mother but rather Tetra her  grandmother this seems to suggest that  tetra might have had a son who 